  "why": [
   "EXT-1 drop_recommend by E: Every distractor is below the key, and a one-line bound read from the white constraint kills all three: 3s <= 49 gives s <= 16, so Mist must supply at least 77 - 16 = 61 L of blue, and m >= 13. Options 2 and 5 die at a glance (they leave 67 or 52 Sky batches, needing 150+ L of white), and the swap distractor 12 dies by the same bound. Key is the largest option, so a student can pick it without solving the system. This is the single-bound / one-sided pattern dropped on earlier batches. A repair needs at least one distractor ABOVE 13 that passes the white cap (for example a wrong-path value between 14 and 15, or a value from a path that raises m), but the brief says re-author rather than fit to this grader."
